	(text "RADIO MEZZANINE J14 - now 2x10 (design review: \"add more grounds to the mezz\nconnectors\", \"maybe add more mezz connectors\" -> one larger connector instead).\n\n   1  +3V3            2  GND\n   3  +3V3            4  GND\n   5  ESP_SPI_SCK     6  GND\n   7  ESP_SPI_MOSI    8  GND\n   9  ESP_SPI_MISO   10  GND\n  11  ESP_SPI_CS     12  GND\n  13  ESP_HANDSHAKE  14  GND\n  15  ESP_DATA_READY 16  GND\n  17  ESP_RST        18  GND\n  19  +3V3           20  GND\n\nWHY: the old 2x5 carried the radio's 650 mA on ONE +3V3 pin and returned it on\ntwo grounds. Now 3 power pins (~215 mA each) and 10 grounds, with a ground\ndirectly opposite every signal so each SPI line has an adjacent return path.\nThat matters - the ESP SPI runs at 15.625 Mbit/s across a board-to-board joint.\n\n>> THE DAUGHTERBOARD MUST MATCH THIS PINOUT. It is not built yet; this is the\n   reference. The old 1..10 pinout in the radio design doc is superseded.\n\nFootprint is still TBD and must be a LATCHING board-to-board / mezzanine part,\nnot a 2.54mm pin header - the radio doc says a plain header \"WILL go loose\nduring comp\"."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 149.86 300.99 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
